# Workspace Filesystem Protocol

Root = directory containing `AGENTS.md`. Plain filesystem I/O. Any capable agent may write behind
`01-agent-controller.mdc` gates.

## Allowed without confirmation

- Read any workspace file for context
- Write artifacts to `05-artifacts/active/` (naming convention)
- Update `06-context/project-context.md`, session fragments, `artifact-registry.md`
- Update skills in `03-skills/` when explicitly requested
- Regenerate: `build-related.py` → `build-registry.py` → `build-trigger-routes.py`

## Requires user confirmation

- Modifying `01-frameworks/` or `04-preferences/user-preferences.md`
- Modifying `00-bootstrap/` (except doctor-driven dist sync Sean requested)
- Deleting or archiving any skill directory
- Hand-editing `.cursor/rules/` outside an explicit Cursor-adapter task

## Obsidian conventions

`[[wikilinks]]` · YAML frontmatter on metadata notes · lowercase-hyphen tags ·
`- [ ]` / `- [x]` · artifact `context_descriptor_vN.N_YYYY-MM-DD.ext` · archive don't delete

## Do not run

`09-tools/compile-cursor-rules.py` is **archived** (`_archive/compile-cursor-rules.py`). It would
overwrite the hand-authored `AGENTS.md` contract. Ignore any stale docs that mention it.
